Z||000004||MrPBody||11-15-2000||08:21 AM||||Here are details: <A HREF="http://fierozone.tripod.com/weekend/swaybar/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://fierozone.tripod.com/weekend/swaybar/index.html</A> <P>Good luck!  I'll probably do this eventually, balanced with a stiffer front bar.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||the need for speed||11-15-2000||02:51 PM||||hey al did you take off the top poly bushing and use a washer instead like it said in the web page.also you said to get the smaller size end link,so my question is ,will the front endlink size work.The web site for installing a rear bar says something about modifying the original size endlink.<p>[This message has been edited by the need for speed (edited 11-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||AL||11-15-2000||10:07 PM||||no i didn't,what i did is find me the smallest bolts that would allow me to fit in all the bushings and still have enough room so that they don't hit the boots,what i did do is cut the center piece in half and it all fit.<B>AL</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif"> <P>------------------<BR> <p>[This message has been edited by AL (edited 11-15-2000).]||||reg||1
